{"name":"Golden Eye","hex":"#ffd789","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"eye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).","The visual sense."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carefully or appraisingly observe (someone or something).","To consider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Eye (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Eye is the fourth album by Thai singer Christina Aguilar, released by GMM Grammy on 25 September 1997.Like her previous three releases, the album sold over 1.7 million copies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dc/Christinagoldeneye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Eye_(album)","wikidata":"Q5579387"},{"title":"GoldenEye","blocks":[{"text":"GoldenEye is a 1995 spy film, the seventeenth in the James Bond series produced by Eon Productions, and the first to star Pierce Brosnan as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond. Directed by Martin Campbell, it was the first in the series not to use any story elements from the works of novelist Ian Fleming. It was also the first James Bond film not produced by Albert R. Broccoli, following his stepping down from Eon Productions and replacement by his daughter, Barbara Broccoli. The story was conceived and written by Michael France, with later collaboration by other writers. In the film, Bond fights to prevent rogue ex-MI6 agent Alec Trevelyan from using a satellite weapon against London to cause a global financial collapse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/24/GoldenEye_-_UK_cinema_poster.jpg/330px-GoldenEye_-_UK_cinema_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GoldenEye","wikidata":"Q19089"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Pierce_Brosnan_2017_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pierce_Brosnan_2017_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Pierce_Brosnan_2017_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pierce_Brosnan_2017_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APierce_Brosnan_2017_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sean_Bean_TIFF_2015.jpg/500px-Sean_Bean_TIFF_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Se